cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "all-research-skills: research tooling skills"
message: "If you use this skill, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucchesi
    given-names: Alessandro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0624-5311"
    affiliation: "IRST \"Dino Amadori\" IRCCS, Meldola, Italy"
abstract: >-
  Skills for preparing a scientific manuscript, built on one principle: a
  plausible detail completed from memory is never accepted in place of a
  retrieved one. bibliography-verification matches every reference against
  PubMed as written, separating out the entries PubMed cannot see rather
  than passing them, and repairs nothing silently. scientific-figures
  compiles a declarative specification into journal-ready vector figures;
  relations carry a mandatory evidence level rendered through a dedicated
  visual channel, so a proposed mechanism cannot be drawn as a demonstrated
  one; pictorial assets resolve against a registry of open-licensed
  libraries under an enforced licence gate; and type size is treated as a
  hard constraint at the target column width.
keywords:
  - reference verification
  - citation integrity
  - scientific illustration
  - graphical abstract
  - mechanism of action
  - pathway diagram
  - reproducible figures
  - open licensing
license: MIT
version: 0.8.0
date-released: "2026-10-11"
